# L2-SYN-028 recovery-landing regression fixture: header-and-sync-recovery.hex
# byte for byte, plus the 0x0000 end-of-records terminator that every DDC
# recording ends with.
#
# Sync recovery lands on the final record. Recovery's look-ahead did not honor
# the terminator anywhere -- the carve-out that stops a mis-aligned candidate
# from validating off a stray zero DATA word -- so a recovered final record
# followed by the terminator failed validation and was silently dropped,
# though the same file without the terminator kept it. A terminator that is
# the last word of the file is honored in recovery too: it carries exactly the
# weight of end-of-file, which recovery already accepts. The expected CSV is
# header-and-sync-recovery's, all three rows.

FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00 FF00

